### --- DUNNING ---
### Dunning has no endpoints of its own: it is a scheduled job
### (dunning.cycle.cron, hourly at :15). What it does is visible through the
### invoice, its payments, and the subscription's status.
###
### The pieces you drive by hand are below: storing the payment method the
### job charges, and watching what each state looks like afterwards.
###
### To see a full cycle without waiting days:
###   1. store pm_card_visa_chargeDeclined for a customer (below)
###   2. create a subscription and force its period closed in psql, then
###      generate an invoice (see billing.http)
###   3. temporarily set dunning.cycle.cron to "*/20 * * * * *" and restart,
###      or just wait for the top-of-hour run
###   4. after the first run: the subscription is PAST_DUE and the invoice
###      still OPEN, with one FAILED payment
###   5. the retry is a day out, so to see attempt 2 immediately:
###        UPDATE dunning_state SET next_attempt_at = now() - interval '1 minute';
###   6. repeat until attempt 4: the invoice becomes UNCOLLECTIBLE and the
###      subscription CANCELED
###   7. or switch the stored method to pm_card_visa before a retry: the
###      invoice goes PAID and the subscription back to ACTIVE


### Auth — acme admin
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/token
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "tenantId": "acme",
  "email": "admin@acme.test",
  "password": "subscriptionhub"
}

> {%
    client.global.set("acmeToken", response.body.token);
%}

### Auth — acme support (read-only role)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/token
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "tenantId": "acme",
  "email": "support@acme.test",
  "password": "subscriptionhub"
}

> {%
    client.global.set("supportToken", response.body.token);
%}

### Auth — demo admin, for the isolation check
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/token
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "tenantId": "demo",
  "email": "admin@demo.test",
  "password": "subscriptionhub"
}

> {%
    client.global.set("demoToken", response.body.token);
%}


### Setup — a customer to collect from. Capture the id.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/customers
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{acmeToken}}

{
  "email": "dunning-demo@acme.test",
  "name": "Dunning Demo Customer"
}

> {%
    client.global.set("dunningCustomerId", response.body.id);
%}


### Store a payment method — a card that always declines, so the next
### billing cycle puts this customer into dunning
### (expects 200 and "hasDefaultPaymentMethod": true; the token itself is
### never echoed back)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/customers/{{dunningCustomerId}}/payment-method
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{acmeToken}}

{
  "paymentMethod": "pm_card_visa_chargeDeclined"
}

### Store a payment method — blank (expects 400 VALIDATION_ERROR)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/customers/{{dunningCustomerId}}/payment-method
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{acmeToken}}

{
  "paymentMethod": ""
}

### Store a payment method — support role (expects 403 ACCESS_DENIED)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/customers/{{dunningCustomerId}}/payment-method
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{supportToken}}

{
  "paymentMethod": "pm_card_visa"
}

### Store a payment method — tenant isolation: acme's customer under demo
### (expects 404 CUSTOMER_NOT_FOUND)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/customers/{{dunningCustomerId}}/payment-method
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{demoToken}}

{
  "paymentMethod": "pm_card_visa"
}

### The customer — expects "hasDefaultPaymentMethod": true and no token
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/customers/{{dunningCustomerId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{acmeToken}}

### Fix the card — what a customer does after a decline. The next dunning
### attempt then succeeds and the subscription recovers.
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/customers/{{dunningCustomerId}}/payment-method
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{acmeToken}}

{
  "paymentMethod": "pm_card_visa"
}

### Remove the stored method — this customer is then never charged
### automatically; their invoices stay OPEN for a human to collect
### (expects 200 and "hasDefaultPaymentMethod": false; calling it twice is
### not an error, because it clears a field rather than deleting a row)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/customers/{{dunningCustomerId}}/payment-method
Authorization: Bearer {{acmeToken}}


### --- Watching the job's effects ---
### Requires {{billingInvoiceId}} and {{billingSubId}} from billing.http.

### The invoice — OPEN while dunning retries, PAID once a retry lands,
### UNCOLLECTIBLE once the attempts run out
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/invoices/{{billingInvoiceId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{acmeToken}}

### Its payments — one FAILED row per attempt, each with its failureCode
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/invoices/{{billingInvoiceId}}/payments
Authorization: Bearer {{acmeToken}}

### The subscription — ACTIVE, then PAST_DUE after the first failure, then
### either ACTIVE again or CANCELED
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/subscriptions/{{billingSubId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{acmeToken}}
